# Security First Rule

Security is enforced by **automated checkers**, not prose. Fix all violations before declaring work done.

**Enforcement:**

| Command | When | What it checks |
| ------- | ---- | -------------- |
| `npm run check:security` | Husky pre-commit, Cursor `afterFileEdit` / `stop` hooks | Static frontend rules (`scripts/check-security.mjs`) |
| `npm run audit` | Quality gate | Dependency vulnerabilities |

---

## Static checker rules (`scripts/check-security.mjs`)

Each violation prints a rule ID. Do not disable rules — fix the code.

| Rule ID | Scope | Violation | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --------- | --- |
| `CRYPTO-NO-MATH-RANDOM` | `services/`, `*-crypto.service.ts` | `Math.random()` | Use `crypto.getRandomValues` / CSPRNG |
| `PERSIST-NO-SECRETS` | `*/stores/` | `partialize` includes secrets | Keep secrets in memory only |
| `HTML-NO-DANGEROUS` | `src/modules/` | `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` | Escape or sanitize HTML |
| `LOG-NO-SECRETS` | `src/modules/`, `src/common/` | `console.*` logs secrets | Remove or redact logs |

---

## Secrets & logging

Never hardcode API keys, tokens, or passwords in source. Use environment variables
(`import.meta.env.VITE_*`) loaded from `.env` (gitignored).

Logs must never contain: passwords, tokens, API keys, or other secrets.

---

## Agent checklist (run on every security-sensitive change)

When editing `src/modules/` or `src/common/`:

1. **Run static checker** — `npm run check:security` must pass.
2. **Run gates** — `npm run typecheck` and `npm run test` for touched modules.
3. **Update docs** — `docs/FRONTEND.mdc` if security-related behavior changes.

If the checker fails, fix the violation — do not bypass or suppress rules.
